    <value>Prevent sleep while work is in progress</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Background_Unattended_PreventSleepExplanation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>While a run, a debate or an audit is in progress, the computer does not sleep because of inactivity. The screen can still turn off. You can put the computer to sleep whenever you want.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_Unattended_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unattended work</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_Unattended_What" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Here you choose what happens when you close the window with work in progress. Agent Studio can keep running in the tray, next to the clock. It can also keep the computer awake, so it does not sleep in the middle of the work.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_Unattended_Actions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose what Agent Studio does when you close the window: ask, keep running in the tray or exit.
Turn on “Prevent sleep while work is in progress” if you leave the computer alone.
Click the tray icon to see the work status.
Press “Save” to apply the changes.</value>
